<title>UK: Esprit Telecom to sell shares in UK and US - paper.</title>
<headline>Esprit Telecom to sell shares in UK and US - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>European telecommunications carrier Esprit Telecom is set to announce an international public offering of shares in New York and London, the Financial Times reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the five-year-old operator had appointed Lehman Brothers as the investment bank to lead the share sale.</p>
<p>Analysts estimated Esprit would have an enterprise value of about $200 million and bankers expected it to raise about $100 million in the offering, said the Financial Times.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 6762</p>
</text>
